+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry is the trust boundary between model-produced JSON and consumer-provided executors. It applies each tool's provider-facing JSON Schema before any application code receives the input.
+
+## Execution contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a tool response describing each `required`, `type`, or `enum` violation before invoking the executor; the description names the property path and failed constraint without including the rejected value. Valid inputs, including undeclared properties, reach the executor unchanged exactly once. ([validated by: validates model input before invoking a tool and preserves valid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L17))
+- An unregistered tool name remains a programmer error: `execute` throws `Unknown tool: <name>` rather than returning a validation response. ([validated by: validates model input before invoking a tool and preserves valid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L17))
+
+## Schema lifecycle
+
+- A static definition's schema is compiled when the tool is registered, so an invalid schema throws an error naming that tool at registration and later calls reuse the compiled schema. A function-valued definition is resolved and validated against its current schema on every call. ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and resolves dynamic schemas per call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L56))
